Number Guessing Game (Java Swing)

A simple Java Swing application wherein a player has to guess a randomly generated number in limited tries and time. The game includes difficulty levels, a countdown timer, and score tracking.

Features:

Difficulty Levels

Easy → 1–50 (10 tries)

Medium → 1–100 (7 tries)

Hard → 1–500 (5 tries)

Countdown Timer

Each round gives 20 seconds for a guess.

Score System

Score increases eachtime you guess correctly.

GUI Built with Swing

Buttons, text boxes, pop-ups, labels, and more

How to Use :
Install Java 8 or higher.

Save the file as:
Game.java


Compile:
javac Game.java

Run:
java Game

How to Play:

Choose your difficulty level.

Type your guess in the input box.

Click Check.

The game tells you if your guess is

Too high
Too low
Correct ✔

Win before you
Run out of tries
Run out of time.

Requirements:
Java JDK 8+
No external libraries needed.

License :
Free to use, modify and learn from.